  "permutation_null": {
   "unit_of_permutation": "TEAM, not player-season. 5,323 rows are only 32 independent units; a row-level shuffle breaks the franchise clustering, manufactures variance the real comparison does not have, and inflates the null. The first version did exactly that and produced an observed TVD BELOW the null mean, which is the tell.",
   "n_bridged_teams": 6,
   "n_teams": 32,
   "n_permutations": 2000,
   "null_mean_tvd": 0.0241,
   "null_p95_tvd": 0.0418,
   "p_value": 0.8535
  },
  "verdict": "NO DIFFERENCE — TVD is within the permutation null",
  "confound_named_in_advance": "Bridged teams are not a random sample. A venue carries an S&P 500 name because the franchise is in a large market with a buyer for the rights, so any difference is a market-size and franchise-age effect before it is anything about sponsorship. This test can detect a difference; it cannot attribute one."
 },
